{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792832411,"nonce":"7zrojdRjVR8hTxim5Lti0N2T7ZE=","title":"Buffers: typed reads and writes from every language","message":"A `caribou.Buffer` over Haxe-owned storage (an hl.Bytes holding f32/f64/i32 component arrays, as ChimpMonk keeps its SoA components) can't be read or written as typed values everywhere:\n- Wren sees a Sequence of bytes.\n- Lua reads it through its string library (`string.unpack`) and can't write it.\n- Python reads the bytes in place but has no typed or writable view (c575125).\n\nWanted, so a script system can step components in place in any language: accessors on the Buffer that every language calls, `getF32/getF64/getI32/getU8(offset)` and the matching setters, bounds-checked and refused on a read-only buffer.\n\nTyped views over external memory (a WrenLift typed array over foreign storage, a Python memoryview cast) are speed-ups on top of these, not the way in.","files":null}]}